	{
		"level": 2, "title": "Making Decisions", "concept": "if / else and switch",
		"pages": [
			{"title": "Customers choose now",
			"text": "No more Today's Special: customers now order [b]anything on the menu[/b], so staff must [b]ask[/b] and then [b]decide[/b] what to cook.\n\nA new customer shows a [b]?[/b] bubble: nobody knows their order yet, and they won't accept food until someone asks.\n\nNew kitchen functions:\n• [b]take_order()[/b] walks to the customer who has waited longest, asks what they want and [b]returns[/b] the dish, like EGSILOG (or NOTHING if no one is waiting). Their bubble then shows the dish, and they wait more patiently.\n• [b]is_burnt()[/b] returns 1 if the food you hold is burnt.\n• [b]trash()[/b] throws away what you hold, at the TRASH.\n\nA function that [b]returns[/b] a value can be stored in a variable.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    int order = take_order();\n    printf(\"Next order: %s\\n\", order);\n}", "w3": "c_conditions.php"},
			{"title": "Comparing values",
			"text": "[b]Comparison operators[/b] compare two values and give [b]1[/b] (true) or [b]0[/b] (false):\n• [b]==[/b] equal to          • [b]!=[/b] not equal to\n• [b]>[/b] greater than       • [b]<[/b] less than\n• [b]>=[/b] greater or equal  • [b]<=[/b] less or equal\n\n[b]Careful:[/b] [b]==[/b] compares; a single [b]=[/b] stores a value. Writing [code]if (order = EGSILOG)[/code] is a classic bug.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    int eggs = 3;\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", eggs > 2);    // 1 (true)\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", eggs == 5);   // 0 (false)\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", eggs != 5);   // 1 (true)\n}", "w3": "c_operators_comparison.php"},
			{"title": "The if statement",
			"text": "[b]if[/b] runs a block of code only when its condition is true.\n\n• The condition goes in ( ) right after if.\n• The code to run goes in { }.\n• If the condition is false, the block is skipped and the program continues after it.\n• Write it in lowercase: [code]If[/code] or [code]IF[/code] is an error.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    int order = take_order();\n    if (order == EGSILOG) {\n        printf(\"I know how to make this!\\n\");\n    }\n    printf(\"Checked the order.\\n\");\n}", "w3": "c_conditions.php"},
			{"title": "else",
			"text": "[b]else[/b] gives a second block that runs when the condition is [b]false[/b]. Exactly one of the two blocks runs.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    if (holding() == NOTHING) {\n        printf(\"Hands are free\\n\");\n    } else {\n        printf(\"Holding %s\\n\", holding());\n    }\n}", "w3": "c_conditions_else.php"},
			{"title": "else if",
			"text": "[b]else if[/b] tests another condition when the ones before it were false.\n\n• Conditions are checked from top to bottom.\n• Only the [b]first[/b] block whose condition is true runs; the rest are skipped.\n• A final [b]else[/b] catches everything that didn't match.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    int order = take_order();\n    if (order == EGSILOG) {\n        printf(\"Egsilog coming up\\n\");\n    } else if (order == HOTSILOG) {\n        printf(\"Hotsilog coming up\\n\");\n    } else if (order == NOTHING) {\n        printf(\"No orders right now\\n\");\n    } else {\n        printf(\"Something else: %s\\n\", order);\n    }\n}", "w3": "c_conditions_elseif.php"},
			{"title": "Logical operators and booleans",
			"text": "Join conditions with [b]logical operators[/b]:\n• [b]&&[/b] and: true only if [b]both[/b] sides are true\n• [b]||[/b] or: true if [b]at least one[/b] side is true\n• [b]![/b] not: flips true and false\n\nA [b]bool[/b] variable holds true or false. Store a test in one to give it a clear name.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    int order = take_order();\n    bool silog = order == EGSILOG || order == HOTSILOG || order == TOCILOG;\n    bool free_hands = holding() == NOTHING;\n    if (silog && free_hands) {\n        printf(\"Start with rice\\n\");\n    }\n    if (!silog) {\n        printf(\"Not a silog\\n\");\n    }\n}", "w3": "c_operators_logical.php"},
			{"title": "Short-hand if (ternary)",
			"text": "For a quick choice between two values there is a short form:\n\n[code]variable = (condition) ? value_if_true : value_if_false;[/code]\n\nUse it for small choices; use a full if / else for steps like go_to() and cook().",
			"code": "void main() {\n    int order = take_order();\n    int price = (order == HOTSILOG) ? 40 : 30;\n    printf(\"Charge %d coins\\n\", price);\n}", "w3": "c_conditions_short_hand.php"},
			{"title": "The switch statement",
			"text": "When you compare [b]one value[/b] against [b]many[/b] possibilities, a long else-if chain gets hard to read. [b]switch[/b] is the tidy way:\n\n• The value in [b]switch ( )[/b] is checked once.\n• It is compared with each [b]case VALUE:[/b] label.\n• The matching case's code runs.\n• Case values must be fixed: numbers, letters like 'A', or kitchen names like EGSILOG.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    int order = take_order();\n    switch (order) {\n        case EGSILOG:\n            printf(\"Egsilog\\n\");\n            break;\n        case HOTSILOG:\n            printf(\"Hotsilog\\n\");\n            break;\n        case TOCILOG:\n            printf(\"Tocilog\\n\");\n            break;\n    }\n}", "w3": "c_switch.php"},
			{"title": "break, default and fall-through",
			"text": "• [b]break;[/b] leaves the switch. If you forget it, the code [b]falls through[/b] and keeps running the next case too!\n• Sometimes that's useful: stack several cases on top of each other to share code.\n• [b]default:[/b] runs when no case matches, like a final else. It's optional but recommended.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    int order = take_order();\n    switch (order) {\n        case EGSILOG:\n        case HOTSILOG:\n        case TOCILOG:\n            printf(\"A silog: start with rice\\n\");   // all three land here\n            break;\n        case NOTHING:\n            printf(\"No customers yet\\n\");\n            break;\n        default:\n            printf(\"Something else: %s\\n\", order);\n    }\n}", "w3": "c_switch.php"},
			{"title": "if or switch?",
			"text": "• Use [b]switch[/b] when you check [b]one variable[/b] against exact values: which dish was ordered.\n• Use [b]if[/b] for ranges and combined conditions: [code]coins >= 100 && eggs > 0[/code].\n\nA full order program: read the order, decide, cook, serve. Press Run again for each new customer (in Lesson 3 loops will do that for you).",
			"code": "void main() {\n    int order = take_order();\n    switch (order) {\n        case EGSILOG:\n            go_to(FRIDGE); pick_up(RICE); go_to(GRILL); cook(); go_to(ASSEMBLY); plate();\n            go_to(FRIDGE); pick_up(EGG); go_to(GRILL); cook(); go_to(ASSEMBLY); plate();\n            assemble(EGSILOG);\n            serve();\n            break;\n        default:\n            printf(\"Can't make %s yet\\n\", order);\n    }\n}", "w3": "c_switch.php"},
			{"title": "Your Level 2 challenges",
			"text": "Three challenges, together with this level's goals (sell dishes, earn profit), unlock the next upgrade (top left). Each pays coins [b]and EXP[/b], and needs a dish served in the same Run:\n• [b]Take an order[/b]: use [b]take_order()[/b] and serve what the customer asked for.\n• [b]Decide with if / else[/b]: an [b]if[/b] with an [b]else[/b] chooses what to cook.\n• [b]Switch on the order[/b]: a [b]switch[/b] with case labels [b]and a default[/b].\nOne program can do all three: take the order, use if / else to check for NOTHING, and switch on the dish.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    int order = take_order();\n    if (order == NOTHING) {\n        printf(\"Nobody is waiting\\n\");\n    } else {\n        switch (order) {\n            case EGSILOG:\n                // make and serve Egsilog\n                break;\n            default:\n                printf(\"Can't make %s yet\\n\", order);\n        }\n    }\n}", "w3": "c_switch.php"},
		],
		"practice": {"task": "Read the next order with take_order(). Use switch to make and serve EGSILOG, HOTSILOG or TOCILOG, and default to print orders you can't make yet.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    int order = take_order();\n    switch (order) {\n        case EGSILOG:\n            // make and serve Egsilog\n            break;\n        case HOTSILOG:\n            // make and serve Hotsilog\n            break;\n        case TOCILOG:\n            // make and serve Tocilog\n            break;\n        default:\n            printf(\"Can't make %s yet\\n\", order);\n    }\n}"},
	},
	{
		"level": 3, "title": "Loops", "concept": "while, do/while and for",
		"pages": [
			{"title": "Why loops?",
			"text": "Pressing Run for every customer gets tiring. A [b]loop[/b] repeats a block of code, so a few lines can serve a whole day of customers.\n\nNew kitchen functions:\n• [b]has_order()[/b] returns 1 while a customer is waiting for someone to take their order.\n• [b]post_order(DISH)[/b] and [b]check_counter()[/b] let two staff work as a team (see \"Teamwork: waiter and cook\").\n• [b]stock(INGREDIENT)[/b] returns how many are left.\n• [b]doneness()[/b] returns 0-100 (how cooked your food is), and [b]flip()[/b] flips it at the GRILL.",
			"code": "", "w3": "c_while_loop.php"},
			{"title": "The while loop",
			"text": "A [b]while[/b] loop repeats its block [b]as long as[/b] its condition is true.\n\n1. Check the condition.\n2. If true: run the block, then go back to step 1.\n3. If false: skip to the code after the loop.\n\nThe condition is checked [b]first[/b], so if it starts false the block never runs.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    int made = 0;\n    while (made < 3) {\n        printf(\"Made %d\\n\", made);\n        made++;\n    }\n    printf(\"Done!\\n\");\n}", "w3": "c_while_loop.php"},
			{"title": "Don't loop forever",
			"text": "Something inside the loop must eventually make the condition false. If [code]made++[/code] were missing, [code]made < 3[/code] would stay true [b]forever[/b]: an [b]infinite loop[/b].\n\nThe game stops a program that loops for too long without doing kitchen work and shows the line, so nothing breaks, but your staff stop working.\n\nA loop that waits for customers is fine, because it does kitchen work (wait) each time.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    int count = 0;\n    while (count < 5) {\n        count++;   // without this line the loop never ends\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", count);\n}", "w3": "c_while_loop.php"},
			{"title": "do / while",
			"text": "[b]do/while[/b] runs the block [b]once first[/b], then checks the condition. It always runs at least once.\n\n[code]do { ... } while (condition);[/code]\n\nNote the semicolon after the closing ). Use it when the steps must happen before you can check, like tasting food before deciding it's done.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    int tries = 0;\n    do {\n        tries++;\n        printf(\"Try %d\\n\", tries);\n    } while (tries < 3);\n}", "w3": "c_do_while_loop.php"},
			{"title": "The for loop",
			"text": "Use [b]for[/b] when you know [b]how many times[/b] to repeat. It packs three parts into one line:\n\n[code]for (statement 1; statement 2; statement 3)[/code]\n• [b]Statement 1[/b] runs [b]once[/b], before the loop: [code]int i = 0[/code]\n• [b]Statement 2[/b] is the condition, checked before [b]every[/b] round: [code]i < 3[/code]\n• [b]Statement 3[/b] runs after [b]every[/b] round: [code]i++[/code]",
			"code": "void main() {\n    for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n        printf(\"Round %d\\n\", i);\n    }\n}", "w3": "c_for_loop.php"},
			{"title": "Tracing a for loop",
			"text": "Follow [code]for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++)[/code] step by step:\n\n• i = 0 → 0 < 3 true → run block → i++ makes 1\n• i = 1 → 1 < 3 true → run block → i becomes 2\n• i = 2 → 2 < 3 true → run block → i becomes 3\n• i = 3 → 3 < 3 [b]false[/b] → loop ends\n\nSo the block ran [b]3[/b] times, with i = 0, 1 and 2. Starting at 0 and using < is the usual pattern.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    // cook two eggs for a Silog Platter\n    for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {\n        go_to(FRIDGE);\n        pick_up(EGG);\n        go_to(STOVE);\n        cook();\n        go_to(ASSEMBLY);\n        plate();\n    }\n}", "w3": "c_for_loop.php"},
			{"title": "Counting other ways",
			"text": "• Count by 2: [code]i += 2[/code]\n• Count down: start high and use [code]i--[/code]\n• Build a total: add to a variable inside the loop.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    int total = 0;\n    for (int i = 5; i > 0; i--) {\n        total += i;\n    }\n    printf(\"5+4+3+2+1 = %d\\n\", total);\n    for (int even = 0; even <= 6; even += 2) {\n        printf(\"%d \", even);\n    }\n}", "w3": "c_for_loop.php"},
			{"title": "Nested loops",
			"text": "A loop can go [b]inside[/b] another loop. The inner loop runs completely for [b]each[/b] round of the outer loop.\n\nIf the outer loop runs 3 times and the inner loop 2 times, the inner block runs 3 × 2 = 6 times. You'll need this for 2D arrays in Lesson 4.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    for (int table = 1; table <= 3; table++) {\n        for (int seat = 1; seat <= 2; seat++) {\n            printf(\"Table %d seat %d\\n\", table, seat);\n        }\n    }\n}", "w3": "c_for_loop_nested.php"},
			{"title": "break and continue",
			"text": "• [b]break[/b] jumps out of the loop completely.\n• [b]continue[/b] skips the rest of this round and starts the next one.\n\nBoth work in while, do/while and for loops.",
			"code": "void main() {\n    for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {\n        if (i == 4) {\n            break;       // stop at 4\n        }\n        if (i == 1) {\n            continue;    // skip 1\n        }\n        printf(\"%d \", i);\n    }\n}", "w3": "c_break_continue.php"},
			{"title": "Loops + decisions: a real shift",
			"text": "Put it together: keep working [b]while[/b] there are orders, and let [b]switch[/b] pick the dish each time. When no one is waiting, wait a second and check again.\n\nCustomers who wait too long leave, so keep your loop busy!",
			"code": "void main() {\n    while (1) {\n        if (has_order()) {\n            int order = take_order();\n            switch (order) {\n                case EGSILOG:\n                    printf(\"Making Egsilog\\n\");\n                    break;\n                default:\n                    printf(\"Making %s\\n\", order);\n            }\n        } else {\n            wait(1);\n        }\n    }\n}", "w3": "c_while_loop.php"},
			{"title": "Teamwork: waiter and cook",
			"text": "John joins the team at this level. Staff become a [b]waiter[/b] or a [b]cook[/b] just by the program you give them: there's no setting, the code decides.\n\n• The [b]waiter[/b] loops: take_order(), walk to the SERVING_COUNTER, and [b]post_order(order)[/b]. Each order becomes a numbered paper ticket at the [b]back[/b] of the line on the counter.\n• A [b]cook[/b] loops: [b]check_counter()[/b] walks to the counter and takes the [b]oldest[/b] ticket, returning its dish (or NOTHING). Then cook it and serve() it: the ticket remembers who ordered.\n\nTickets come off the counter in the same order they went on: [b]first in, first out[/b]. That's called a [b]queue[/b], like the line at a shop. Watch the ticket numbers 1, 2, 3 above the counter.\n\nNo waiter? Cooks can still take_order() themselves, it's just slower. Try both and compare!",
			"code": "// Give this to John (the waiter)\nvoid main() {\n    while (1) {\n        if (has_order()) {\n            int order = take_order();\n            go_to(SERVING_COUNTER);\n            post_order(order);\n        } else {\n            wait(1);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// Give this to Jane (the cook), in her own program:\n// while (1) {\n//     int order = check_counter();\n//     if (order == NOTHING) { wait(1); }\n//     else { ...make it, assemble(order); serve(); }\n// }", "w3": "c_while_loop.php"},
			{"title": "Your Level 3 challenges",
			"text": "Three challenges (coins [b]and EXP[/b] each), all in a Run that serves food. This level's goals ask you to sell 8 of each new dish and earn 1000 profit:\n• [b]Busy shift[/b]: serve [b]3 dishes in one Run[/b]. Only a loop can do that.\n• [b]Count with a for loop[/b]: a [b]for[/b] loop that repeats at least twice.\n• [b]Waiter + cook[/b]: a cook takes a ticket with [b]check_counter()[/b] and serves it, while another staff member posts tickets with [b]post_order()[/b].\nTip: a cook that loops [code]for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++)[/code] over tickets finishes all three at once.",
			"code": "// Cook: three tickets, one for loop\nvoid main() {\n    for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n        int order = check_counter();\n        while (order == NOTHING) {\n            wait(1);\n            order = check_counter();\n        }\n        // switch (order) { ...make it... serve(); }\n    }\n}", "w3": "c_for_loop.php"},
		],
		"practice": {"task": "Write a program that keeps serving: while (1), if has_order() take take_order() and switch on it to make and serve each dish on your menu; otherwise wait(1).",
			"code": "void main() {\n    while (1) {\n        if (has_order()) {\n            int order = take_order();\n            switch (order) {\n                case EGSILOG:\n                    // make Egsilog, then serve()\n                    break;\n                case HAMBURGER:\n                    // make Hamburger, then serve()\n                    break;\n                default:\n                    printf(\"Skipping %s\\n\", order);\n            }\n        } else {\n            wait(1);\n        }\n    }\n}"},
